  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "BC extends the integral toolkit with integration by parts, partial fractions, and improper integrals over infinite or unbounded intervals.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Three new tools",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>By parts</strong>: \\( \\displaystyle\\int u\\,dv=uv-\\int v\\,du \\). <strong>Partial fractions</strong> split a rational integrand into simpler pieces. <strong>Improper integrals</strong> are limits: \\( \\displaystyle\\int_a^{\\infty} f=\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\int_a^{b} f \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "By parts",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( uv-\\displaystyle\\int v\\,du \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Partial fractions",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{(x-a)(x-b)} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Improper",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\int_a^b f \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arctangent",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dx}{x^{2}+a^{2}}=\\dfrac1a\\arctan\\dfrac{x}{a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example · By parts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int x e^{x}\\,dx \\) with \\( u=x,\\ dv=e^{x}dx \\). \\[ x e^{x}-\\int e^{x}\\,dx=(x-1)e^{x}+C. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Integration by parts",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int x^2 e^x\\,dx\\). <p>Apply IBP twice. Let \\(u=x^2,\\,dv=e^x dx\\): \\(x^2e^x-2\\int xe^x dx\\).</p><p>For \\(\\int xe^x dx\\): \\(u=x,\\,dv=e^x dx\\Rightarrow xe^x-e^x\\).</p>\\[\\int x^2e^x\\,dx=x^2e^x-2xe^x+2e^x+c=e^x(x^2-2x+2)+c.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Determine whether \\(\\displaystyle\\int_1^\\infty\\frac{1}{x^2}\\,dx\\) converges, and if so find its value.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\int_1^b\\frac{1}{x^2}dx=\\left[-\\frac{1}{x}\\right]_1^b=1-\\frac{1}{b}\\to1\\) as \\(b\\to\\infty\\). Converges to \\(1\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
